`.\n   - [`yang.clojure`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L62-L265) defines `call-site-key` (`:yang/call-site`), `call-site-version` (`1`), `*call-site-finalizing*` ([`yang/clojure.cljc:72-76`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L72-L76)), [`eligible-application-sites`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L93-L100), [`call-site-metadata`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L103-L115) (sorted deterministically with `jing/canonical-compare`), [`marked-application-sites`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L118-L127), [`validate-call-site-coverage!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L140-L250) (supporting transport-deduped mode, `:declared? true`, and `:per-occurrence-origins? true` with multi-claim refusal `:yang/call-site-multi-claim` at [`yang/clojure.cljc:210-216`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L210-L216)), and [`validate-ast-call-sites!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L253-L264).\n   - Every public Clojure compilation entry point finalizes its returned map AST with `annotate-call-sites`:\n     - [`compile-form`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L2249-L2262) (via `*call-site-finalizing*` outer guard) and [`compile`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L3068-L3091).\n     - [`compile-program`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L2392-L2625) (annotated at [`:2459`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L2459) on both `:native` and `:arg-vector`/`:outcomes` paths, including when `:bundle-prelude? true` bundles `yang.core.call/uast` and `yang.clojure.prelude/uast`).\n     - [`lower-unit`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L3224-L3255) (re-annotated at [`:3255`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L3255) after [`publish-to-globals`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L3171-L3221) rewrites top-level definitions/reads into `clj/define-global!` and `clj/global-get` applications).\n   - Published Clojure runtime modules and donor kits are C1-finalized:\n     - [`yang.clojure.prelude/module-uast`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc#L108-L112) (`clj` module).\n     - [`yang.core.call/module-uast`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc#L168-L175) (`yang.call` module). *(Note: [`yang.core.call/uast`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc#L158-L165) itself is not wrapped in `u/annotate-call-sites`; Clojure's `compile-program` annotates the whole combined tree at `:2459`, whereas non-Clojure callers of `call/uast` receive unannotated AST until their own seats adopt C1.)*\n     - Exception-kit Clojure donor publications finalized in `b0463cd2` ([`test/yang/call/conformance.clj:99-106`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/call/conformance.clj#L99-L106), [`test/yang/call/exception_legs.clj:79-85`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/call/exception_legs.clj#L79-L85), [`test/yang/call/exception_probes.clj:81-87`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/call/exception_probes.clj#L81-L87)).\n   - REPL frontend catalog manifest updated in [`yin.repl.frontends/clojure-manifest`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc#L42-L60) (`:yang.frontend/revision \"c1-1\"`, `:yang.frontend/support-profile :yang.clojure/c1`).\n\n2. **Encoder boundary enforcement \u0026 per-member claim propagation (`src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc`)**:\n   - [`marked-call-sites`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc#L237-L261) and [`check-call-site-claim!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc#L264-L294) validate every member's C1 claim before stripping `:yang/call-site` from canonical AST rows.\n   - [`program-batch`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc#L297-L345) emits `frontend-metadata` (`[[[:yang/call-site 1] #{[root path] ...}] ...]`) and appends the 6th slot `call-site-claims` (`[bool ...]`) to `[:yin.program/batch ...]` when any member claims C1.\n\n3. **Macro expansion provenance, packet lineage, and post-expansion C1 finalization (`src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc`)**:\n   - Implements Owner Ruling U1–U3 ([`1795310000000-owner-ruling-occurrence-identity-unitarity.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1795310000000-owner-ruling-occurrence-identity-unitarity.md#L1-L33)): threads construction-time `::origin-of` metadata ([`yin/vm/macro.cljc:609-624`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc#L609-L624)), strips tracking metadata before `:data`/`:key` hashing ([`strip-tracking`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc#L635-L659)), preserves packet decomposition/reassembly lineage ([`register-lineage!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc#L670-L681), [`lineage-origin-for`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc#L684-L714), single choke point [`recover-rebuilt-packet`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc#L903-L907)), records 12-slot [`event-row`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc#L1290-L1304) with [`output-correspondence`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc#L1366-L1389), validates post-expansion C1 coverage in [`expand-batch`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc#L1630-L1745) with [`final-call-site-metadata`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc#L1598-L1627), and retains side tables on the expander consumer keyed by `[admission-origin final-root]` ([`call-site-table`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc#L1842-L1856), [`load`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc#L1859-L1882)).\n\n4. **Module publication \u0026 side-table custody (`src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc`)**:\n   - [`publish-closure!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc#L242-L386) enforces C1 coverage on `:clojure` modules, mints scoped admission tokens ([`admission-scope`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc#L123-L136), [`publication-origin`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc#L164-L177)), keeps `:yin.module/call-sites` out of the schema-1 hashed manifest (`83b52a0b`, [`publish.cljc:345-378`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc#L345-L378)), materializes the side-table entity and `:yang.call-site/schema 1` record naming `:yang.call-site/manifest`, and exposes [`published-call-site-table`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc#L434-L480).\n\n5. **Focused test suite (`test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc`)**:\n   - 14 `deftest`s ([`clojure_callsite_test.cljc:99-1238`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc#L99-L1238)) pinning static coverage, boundary validation, macro provenance, twin identical content, encoder per-member claims, packet reassembly provenance, and publisher scope admission identity.\n\n### 1.2 What `cc1` Did NOT Cover (Remaining from Design §3.2 and §5.3)\n\n| Design Surface ([`1794670000000`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md)) | Current State on `master` (`8cd9fc92`) | Exact File \u0026 Line Citations |\n|---|---|---|\n| **§3.2 Row 5 / §2.4**: Projected `{:root :rows}` member in `encoder/project-member` | Drops `:frontend-metadata` uncon