racle_tables.clj, latte_oracle_test.clj, slice9_site_tables.edn)\n```\n\n- **Parallelism**:\n  - `cc2` (transform/REPL preservation) and `cc3` (linearize/derive provenance + oracle `K` bridge) touch disjoint functions (except a small localization in `publish.cljc`: `:312` in `publish-closure!` vs. `:487-635` in `module-from-index`) and can be developed in sequence or parallel, with `cc4` and `D1` sequenced after `cc3`.\n- **Cross-Seat Conflict Check**:\n  1. **`R3` (Exception Uniformity track, `exception-r3-impl` commit `69e7f666`)**:\n     - `69e7f666` modifies [`src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc) heavily (405 insertions, 246 deletions around try/catch/throw/outcomes lowering) and [`test/yang/clojure_test.clj`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/clojure_test.clj).\n     - **Impact**: None of `cc2`, `cc3`, `cc4`, or `D1` needs to edit `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc`! All `yang.clojure` compiler C1 hooks landed in `cc1`. Keeping `cc2`–`cc4` and `D1` out of `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc` guarantees **zero merge conflict** with the exception-track seat's `R3`/`R4` work.\n  2. **`src/cljc/yang/core/prelude.cljc` (owned by PHP/TS seat)**:\n     - Neither `cc2`–`cc4` nor `D1` touches `src/cljc/yang/core/prelude.cljc` (Clojure uses `src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc` and `src/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc`, both already C1-annotated in `cc1`).\n\n---\n\n## 6. Owner Decisions Required Before Dispatch\n\n1. **Resolution of the Handoff vs. Design Decomposition Conflict (Section 2.1)**:\n   - Confirm that the outgoing handoff's parenthetical (*\"the three-kind correspondence: ambient literals, context-API carriers, delegation exclusion\"*) was a misattribution of the already-landed `attribution-as-query` oracle round (`d794382e`/`0f04212b`), and rule whether to execute:\n     - **Option A (Recommended)**: The 3-round Clojure pipeline completion (`cc2` transform/REPL preservation -\u003e `cc3` lowering provenance